+
+        <p>
+        Consent enforcement is the process of ensuring that the rules of pertinent consents are applied 
+        to data access (or other actions such as procedure in the case of treatment consents). This requires 
+        (a) identifying the parameters of the action and its context (e.g., the actor, the purpose of use, 
+        the requested data, etc.), 
+        (b) finding consents that are applicable to the context of requested access, 
+        (c) evaluating the consent rules against the context of access to reach a decision, and 
+        (d) ensuring that the decision is applied (e.g., data access is permitted or denied). 
+        The first three steps are sometimes recognized as a distinct function, known as "consent decision."
+        </p>
+
         <p>
-The enforcement of the Privacy Consent Directive is not included but is expected that 
-enforcement can be done using a mix of the various Access Control enforcement methodologies 
